60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Candidate B, Night Service Extension, is impossible. The rosters are empty.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Candidate A, Crosstown Bus, failed before. The lanes were returned to mixed traffic.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Candidate C, Station Access, is risky. The pre-war shells have hidden voids and high contingency.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Candidate D, Integrated Fare, is expensive. The ticketing fees are already too high.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Candidate C is the only one that addresses the actual time cost, which is waiting.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, but the maintenance contract for lifts has spare capacity. That helps C.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, the accessibility records show four lift rebuilds finished on time. That is good.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, the joint operators' minutes show roadway consents are delegated. That helps A.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Takumi, the old pilots show the late-evening service was viable. But we have no staff.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, the journey audits prove the waiting is the problem. C fixes the flow.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I am leaning towards C. The lift maintenance has spare crew, unlike the rosters.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"I am worried about A, but C has a track record of finishing on time.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"C is risky, but the other options have worse blockers. I will vote C.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"The budget is tight, but C is the only one that doesn't require new staff immediately.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I am voting C. It fixes the real problem of waiting time.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
